            <div xml:id="d21">

                <pb facs="0052" n="44" sameAs="frus:frus1938v01/pg44"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">741.65/549: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-04-25T17:00:00+01:00">April 25, 1938—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 25—2:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>650. The British Ambassador told me today that Hore-Belisha<anchor n="70"
                        xml:id="d21-f1"/> who left here at noon for London was enthusiastic over his
                    Rome visit. He said that Mussolini had been most cordial and that the atmosphere
                    had completely changed as regards Italian feeling towards England. He said that
                    he had found genuine apprehension in Rome regarding future relations with
                    Germany. He had gathered the impression that the Franco-Italian discussions were
                    going satisfactorily and that after Ciano’s return from Albania they would be
                    concluded without difficulty.</p>
                <p>A friend who saw Hore-Belisha off at the air port was told by him that in his
                    talk with Daladier last night he had urged that the French be as reasonable as
                    the British in forthcoming negotiations and that he had in mind particularly
                    negotiations with Germany.</p>
                <p>Copies to London, Berlin and Rome.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d21-f1" n="70" xml:id="d21-f1-content">
                <p>Leslie Hore-Belisha, British Secretary of State for War.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
